            0.294
          ],
          "content": "8. Determine the formula unit mass of the following substances."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.296,
            0.887,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "(i) Ammonium nitrate $\\mathrm{(NH_{4}NO_{3})}$ , used as a nitrogen fertiliser, which is essential for plant growth."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.266,
            0.329,
            0.887,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Phosphoric acid $(  H _3 PO _4 )$ , used to make phosphate fertiliser and detergents."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.364,
            0.888,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Sodium hydrogencarbonate $(NaHCO_{3})_{2}$ , used to relieve acidity and helps in digestion."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.4,
            0.848,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "9. Write the formulae for the compounds formed by the reaction of:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.422,
            0.535,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "(i) Magnesium and nitrogen"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.439,
            0.504,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Lithium and nitrogen"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.456,
            0.478,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "(iii) Sodium and sulfur"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.262,
            0.472,
            0.521,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "(iv) Aluminium and oxygen"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.227,
            0.492,
            0.888,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": "10. Complete the Table 9.3 by writing the formulae of the compounds formed by the cations on the left and the anions at the top. LiNO is given as an example."
